{
  "contract": "public-rank-row-eligibility-roi-pnl@1",
  "description": "One row matrix evaluated by every layer that decides row eligibility: arena.leaderboard_rank_row_is_public_eligible (PG17, before and after 20261122201611), the reader predicate isPublicRankingRowEligible, and the writer projection classifyPublishableRow. `before` is the four-metric policy, `after` the ROI + PnL policy. `worker` is 'same' when the writer verdict equals `after`, 'empties_metric' when the writer publishes the row with the offending metric emptied (so the written row is a different, eligible row), and 'not_applicable' when the case is about a column the writer always sets itself (computed_at). `reader` (optional) is the reader verdict where it differs from `after`: the reader predicate has never re-checked the ROI / PnL range (it only reads rows the database view already served), which this change leaves as it is.",
